[Unit]
Description=Hapax live quota/resource telemetry writer (routing Phase 0.4 / R3 slice)
Documentation=file://%h/.cache/hapax/source-activation/worktree/scripts/hapax-quota-telemetry-writer
After=hapax-secrets.service
OnFailure=notify-failure@%n.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
# Refreshes per-provider platform capability receipts (quota stale_after=15m —
# the paired timer fires every 10m to stay inside that window) and rebuilds the
# live quota/spend ledger at ~/.cache/hapax/orchestration/quota-spend-ledger-live.json,
# which load_dispatch_policy_sources prefers over the checked-in fixtures.
# Credential use (review findings on #4665, rounds 2-3, re-measured against
# scripts/hapax-agy-reviewer): the step-0 pull-forward hosts the agy admission
# chain (hapax-determine → hapax-agy-quota-admission → reviewer smoke), whose
# credential surface is the operator's FILE-BACKED agy login —
# ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/antigravity-oauth-token — which the chain copies
# into a temporary isolated HOME for the smoke invocation (HOME/XDG_* are
# rewritten into the sandbox; the chain's environment allowlist drops provider
# variables). This is the same file-backed login hapax-determine.service uses
# (that unit deliberately has NO EnvironmentFile); the EnvironmentFile below
# feeds the writer's OTHER steps, not the agy chain. No secret VALUES are
# persisted anywhere: receipts carry secret_source names with
# secret_value_persisted=false.
ExecStart=%h/.cache/hapax/source-activation/worktree/.venv/bin/python %h/.cache/hapax/source-activation/worktree/scripts/hapax-quota-telemetry-writer
WorkingDirectory=%h/.cache/hapax/source-activation/worktree
Environment=HOME=%h
Environment=PYTHONPATH=%h/.cache/hapax/source-activation/worktree
EnvironmentFile=-/run/user/1000/hapax-secrets.env
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal
SyslogIdentifier=hapax-quota-telemetry
# On the overlap tick where this unit wins the producer lock, it hosts the
# agy producer chain (hapax-determine → hapax-agy-quota-admission → reviewer
# smoke) that normally runs under hapax-determine.service's 512M cgroup.
# Measured evidence (review findings on #4665, rounds 2-3), recheck with
# `systemctl --user show -p MemoryMax hapax-quota-telemetry.service hapax-determine.service`.
# CAVEAT FIRST (review finding on #4665, round 4): 768M is a judgment call,
# not an evidence-derived ceiling. hapax-determine.service took a cgroup OOM
# kill at 2026-09-12T14:59:26Z under 512M (journal: kernel OOM, unit context)
# — the demonstrated spike exceeds the additive estimate below, so this unit
# inherits a ceiling the evidence already showed insufficient once. Raised
# 512M → 768M to clear the demonstrated spike by ~256 MiB; follow-up: profile
# the determine spike's source (likely the agy smoke's node/python chain)
# before treating 768M as settled. The additive estimate it clears:
# `systemd-run -p MemoryPeak`: writer-alone tick peak 191 MiB, determine tick
# peak 217 MiB (both 2026-09-12); the combined tick runs them IN SERIES in
# one cgroup (~408 MiB additive).
# POST-MERGE ACTIVATION (claude-1 minor, #4665 round 8 — previously recorded
# only in PR prose): after this unit file lands, run
# `systemctl --user daemon-reload`, then recheck BOTH ceilings took effect:
# `systemctl --user show hapax-quota-telemetry.service -p MemoryMax -p TimeoutStartUSec`
# — expected MemoryMax=805306368 (768M) and TimeoutStartUSec=15min. The unit
# sets TimeoutStartSec=900, which systemd RENDERS as TimeoutStartUSec=15min
# (900s = 15min = 900000000us — all three name the same ceiling; compare
# values, not renderings) (claude-1 minor, #4665 round 10). The old
# 256M/3min ceilings timeout-kill a pull-forward tick before the rc=4 surface
# can report; without the recheck the merged fix is inert on any host still
# running the pre-merge unit. If the timer can fire between the activation
# script resync and the daemon-reload (scripts and unit propagate together;
# the recheck must precede the next timer fire), mask the timer across the
# activation window so the first heavier pull-forward tick never runs under
# the old ceilings.
# Recheck after any suspected skipped mint:
# `journalctl --user -u hapax-quota-telemetry.service --since -1d | grep -i oom`.
MemoryMax=768M
# Step 0 of the writer pulls the determination producer forward (child budgets:
# 90s lock wait + 90s producer run ≤ a 210s pull timeout) before the receipt
# refresh (bounded by its own 360s outer timeout), in series. The BOUNDED
# worst-case serial path of those two subprocess budgets is 210s + 360s = 570s
# against the 600s timer cadence; TestPullForwardBudgetPins in tests/scripts/
# test_hapax_quota_telemetry_writer.py re-derives this from the unit files and
# the writer constants, so the arithmetic cannot drift silently. This does NOT
# bound the tick end to end (review finding on #4665, round 3): the receipt
# scans and the two ledger passes sit outside those subprocess budgets — a
# tick that crosses the next cadence boundary DEFERS that fire (systemd will
# not overlap a oneshot unit), which is a silently skipped write cycle. The
# live ledger lock wait itself is bounded (120s, round 4): expiry exits rc=2
# instead of hanging into this unit's TimeoutStartSec. The deferral is
# not covered by duration arithmetic; it is covered by the exit predicate
# below, which is why the predicate — not this comment — is the contract.
#
# Exit codes are the machine-checkable surface (review findings on #4665,
# rounds 3-4): 0 = healthy tick; 1 = pass-2 ledger rebuild failed (pass-1
# ledger stays on disk); 2 = the live ledger lock stayed held past its 120s
# bound (this tick wrote no ledger); 3 = receipt refresh failed; 4 = DEGRADED
# — one of four flap witnesses fired: the embedded agy admission will not
# cover the next publication deadline (admission_freshness_at_publication_s <
# FRESHNESS_HORIZON_S = 819s: one 600s cycle + 60s timer accuracy + 4s
# pre-mint scan bound + bounded pre-write work), OR the tick published after
# the previously published admission expired (admission_continuity_gap_s > 0:
# the surface was dead for the gap even though this tick's own predicate
# passed), OR the capability-receipt surface went dark between the
# predecessor receipts' expiry and the refresh's replacement landing
# (receipt_continuity_gap_s > 0, scoped to the platforms the refresh
# REPUBLISHED: quota routing consumed a dead receipt surface for the gap
# even though every ledger witness passed — critical finding on #4665,
# round 8, C1; lingering retired receipts the refresh never touches are a
# maintenance defect for the capability-surface claim, not this witness), OR
# the pre-mint force-decision scan overran
# its bound (pre_mint_scan_elapsed_s > 4s), which invalidates the horizon
# derivation itself. In all of these the quota surface vouches past evidence
# that died before the next write lands, or did. A DEGRADED tick
# still writes its honest ledger — consumers see true fresh_until, never an
# overclaim — and OnFailure=notify-failure@%n.service surfaces the rc=4, so
# the flap condition this PR repairs cannot ride green in systemd monitoring.
# (rc=4 never fires under --skip-receipts — the tests' diagnostic mode that
# skips the pull and refresh; production ExecStart never passes it.)
# Recheck: `journalctl --user -u hapax-quota-telemetry.service --since -1d |
# grep -E 'DEGRADED|rc=4'` and `scripts/hapax-quota-telemetry-writer --json`
# (summary keys admission_freshness_at_publication_s vs freshness_horizon_s,
# admission_continuity_gap_s, receipt_continuity_gap_s,
# pre_mint_scan_elapsed_s vs pre_mint_scan_bound_s).
# TimeoutStartSec=900 bounds the kill so a wedged tick cannot linger past one
# deferred cycle.
TimeoutStartSec=900
# Killswitch: `systemctl --user mask hapax-quota-telemetry.timer` stops the
# writer; receipts then lapse after quota stale_after (15m) and the live ledger
# goes stale after its TTL — the dispatcher falls back to fail-closed HOLDs,
# never to silently trusting old telemetry.
